& [AuthorityThreats]
  + fixture commission laundering can turn supplied text into physical authority
  + self-issued subject identity can collapse operator and broker roles
  + stale implementation bookend plan preparation Phase3A or expected-current identity can execute superseded work
  + mitigation is exact distinct roles artifact-bound lineage private permit and later external activation record

& [LeaseAndLedgerThreats]
  + missing exclusive share denial permits concurrent brokers
  + lease release before evidence or consumption creates a mutation gap
  + create-new runtime ledger can report flushed content while losing directory-entry durability
  + existing Claimed ledger reset or retry can duplicate effects
  + mitigation is pre-existing lease and fixed ledger continuous handle second observation in-place fixed transition flush reopen byte verification and permanent no-retry

& [SpawnThreats]
  + ordinary child may execute or spawn descendants before job assignment
  + command-line ambiguity can execute a prefix executable
  + inheritable ambient handles can leak authority into children
  + resume count zero greater than one or failure can leave an unexpected execution state
  + mitigation is non-null application CreateProcessW mutable exact command line suspended creation exact attribute handle list assign-before-resume and require resume result one

& [JobThreats]
  + breakaway flags or invalid nested-job hierarchy can escape containment
  + killing only direct child can leave descendants
  + closing job before output readers finish can hide late output
  + trusting summary counts can miss active descendants
  + mitigation is no breakaway kill-on-close whole-job termination query basic accounting zero-active gate bounded readers and terminal close order

& [EnvironmentAndPathThreats]
  + inherited credential proxy Git helper editor pager or current-drive state can widen behavior
  + path aliases reparse points parent traversal case drift or D-drive coordinates can escape scratch
  + schema CODEX_HOME or evidence overlap can corrupt authority inputs
  + mitigation is env-clear exact sorted names canonical nonlink topology strict descendants disjoint roles and before-after identities

& [TranscriptThreats]
  + unknown duplicate reordered late mismatched or oversized frames can make the command consequences ambiguous
  + outer App Server can attempt unadmitted provider thread turn MCP browser network or filesystem behavior
  + denied response may disclose sentinel content or create the canary
  + mitigation is exact six outbound six incoming grammar method closure output bounds post-inventory canary proof and ambiguity quarantine

& [EvidenceThreats]
  + overwrite cleanup truncation or partial writes can erase failure truth
  + summary receipt without raw event digests can conceal order drift
  + verifier that invokes the broker can turn review into a second attempt
  + mitigation is pre-existing attempt directory create-new append-only artifacts ordered event digests read-only independent verifier and no cleanup

& [ResourceThreats]
  + output pipe deadlock timeout overflow process storm or late descendant can hang the host
  + broad builds under low capacity can destabilize the workstation
  + mitigation is concurrent bounded drain threads exact time limits job active and total limits cached focused gates and no cleanup compaction WSL compile or fallback

& [UnsafeAndHandleThreats]
  + raw Windows handles double close leak or use-after-close can defeat kill-on-close
  + panic between suspended creation and job assignment can strand a child
  + mitigation is minimal audited RAII wrappers invalid-handle checks ownership transfer unwind termination and adversarial fake call-order tests

& [Residual]
  + App Server outer-process AppContainer restricted-token and machine-wide firewall isolation are not proved
  + authentic operator commission prepared broker files current Phase3A adequate capacity and one live host attempt remain future evidence
  + SWA-06B independent review signing persistence activation and provider-backed product work remain downstream
